success: true
exit_code: 0
----- stdout -----
Inspect recorded audit history and diffs

Usage: auditstream history [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --config <PATH>
          Path to the configuration file (defaults to ./auditstream.toml if present)
          
          [env: AUDITSTREAM_CONFIG=]

      --table <SCHEMA.TABLE>
          Filter by audited table (`<schema>.<table>`)

      --database-url <URL>
          Postgres connection URL (also reads `DATABASE_URL` as fallback)
          
          [env: AUDITSTREAM_DATABASE_URL]

      --record-id <VALUE>
          Filter by primary key value (requires `--table`; parsed as JSON first, else string)

      --actor <ID>
          Filter by actor identifier (matches `actor.id` or `actor.onBehalfOf.id`)

      --schema <SCHEMA>
          Audit schema name (defaults to `auditstream`)
          
          [env: AUDITSTREAM_SCHEMA=]

      --since <TIME>
          Inclusive lower bound on `occurred_at` (RFC 3339 timestamp or `YYYY-MM-DD` UTC)

  -v, --verbose...
          Increase log verbosity (`-v` info, `-vv` debug)

  -q, --quiet
          Silence warnings and info logs (errors only)

      --until <TIME>
          Exclusive upper bound on `occurred_at` (RFC 3339 timestamp or `YYYY-MM-DD` UTC)

      --limit <N>
          Maximum number of events to return (`1..=1000`)
          
          [default: 100]

      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format (`table` or `json`)

          Possible values:
          - table: Human-readable column table (omits `before` and `after`)
          - json:  One compact JSON event per line matching `spec/schemas/event.schema.json`
          
          [default: table]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

